{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1013","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1013","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1013\",\"parent_revision\":\"e0672fe58ae218c57e1204031d384279c4ec1c7ffe2ec2fc60ff0b5b406a4d1d\",\"root_revision\":\"e0672fe58ae218c57e1204031d384279c4ec1c7ffe2ec2fc60ff0b5b406a4d1d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ngroom-milestone/SKILL.md Step 9 documents the function signature as write_dispatch_plan(milestone, conflict_groups, waves, quality_gates) but the actual Python function in dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py takes a single DispatchPlan model: write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path). An agent following the skill literally would call it incorrectly.\\n\\nFound by codebase-analyzer during #1010 grooming (concern #2).\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: groom-milestone SKILL.md Step 9 should use MCP dispatch tools\\nGoal: Add MCP tool for dispatch plan creation and update SKILL.md Step 9 to use it\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Existing dispatch MCP tools and their capabilities | AVAILABLE | Citation: dispatch-tools-researcher found 4 tools (wave_start, item_status, wave_status, spawn) + dispatch_read\\n2. write_dispatch_plan Python function signature and location | AVAILABLE | Citation: yaml_writer.py:63 \u2014 `def write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) -> Path:`\\n3. DispatchPlan model structure | AVAILABLE | Citation: dispatch_schema/core/models.py defines DispatchPlan\\n4. Current SKILL.md Step 9 content | AVAILABLE | Citation: skill-step9-reader confirmed Step 9 references dispatch_wave_start correctly\\n5. Where to add new MCP tool | AVAILABLE | Citation: dispatch-tools-researcher found existing tools in backlog_core/dispatch.py\\n6. How FastMCP tools are defined in this codebase | AVAILABLE | Citation: existing dispatch tools follow FastMCP v3 patterns\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE, no MISSING inputs\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **groom-milestone skill.md documents wrong write_dispatch_plan function signature** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Codebase analysis \u2014 #1010 Phase 2, concern #2\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThe groom-milestone skill produces a dispatch plan (conflict groups, wave assignments, quality gates) but has no MCP tool to persist it. The orchestrator currently has two options, both wrong:\\n1. Call `write_dispatch_plan()` Python function directly \u2014 violates the architecture (orchestrator should only use MCP tools)\\n2. Write YAML directly \u2014 violates the architecture for the same reason\\n\\nTo observe: run `/groom-milestone {N}` through Steps 5-9. At Step 9, the skill must persist the dispatch plan. No MCP tool exists for this operation. The four existing dispatch tools handle wave *execution* (start, status, spawn), not plan *creation*.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 Agents following this skill literally will construct wrong function arguments or fail to locate the correct API to call. The SKILL.md references writing a dispatch plan but does not document how to construct or pass arguments to the writer function. This creates ambiguity that agents must resolve by inference rather than documented specification.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nAgents following groom-milestone skill literally will:\\n- Search for a write function that accepts `(milestone, conflict_groups, waves, quality_gates)` parameters (inferred from earlier sections mentioning these entities)\\n- Fail to find such a function signature\\n- Either invent incorrect call syntax or escalate for clarification\\n- In worst case, construct `DispatchPlan` incorrectly if they do locate the actual function\\n\\nThe skill describes the WHAT (write a dispatch plan) but not the HOW (call `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path)`). Agents cannot execute without both.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nTwo changes needed:\\n1. **New MCP tool**: Add a `dispatch_create_plan` (or similar) MCP tool to the backlog server that wraps `write_dispatch_plan()` \u2014 accepts conflict groups, wave assignments, quality gates as parameters, constructs the DispatchPlan model internally, and persists it (YAML or database)\\n2. **SKILL.md update**: Update groom-milestone SKILL.md Step 9 to call the new MCP tool instead of describing direct YAML writing or Python function calls\\n\\nThe wave execution tools (dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn) are complete and correct \u2014 no changes needed there.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**New/modified files:**\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch.py` \u2014 add `dispatch_create_plan` MCP tool\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 update Step 9 to call `dispatch_create_plan`\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` \u2014 add tests for new tool\\n\\n**Read-only (no changes):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` \u2014 internal implementation called by new tool\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 DispatchPlan model\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- **#986** (dispatch orchestration MCP tools) \u2014 COMPLETE, provides the foundation. New tool extends this work.\\n- **#934** (Create /groom-milestone skill) \u2014 open P0. The SKILL.md update in this item is part of #934's scope. This item (#1013) can be worked independently or folded into #934.\\n- **dispatch_schema package** \u2014 DispatchPlan model and write_dispatch_plan function already exist and are tested.\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\nAPPROVED \u2014 The gap is clear: dispatch wave execution has MCP tools but dispatch plan creation does not. One new MCP tool + one SKILL.md update. All prerequisite code (DispatchPlan model, write_dispatch_plan function, FastMCP patterns) already exists.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (will use new tool)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` Step 9 \u2014 update to call new MCP tool\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 verify it references MCP tools for dispatch plan reading (uses dispatch_read already)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 New MCP tool needed\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch.py` \u2014 add `dispatch_create_plan` tool wrapping `write_dispatch_plan()`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py::write_dispatch_plan` \u2014 internal implementation, no changes needed (already correct)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py::DispatchPlan` \u2014 model consumed by new tool, no changes needed\\n\\n### Documentation (will need updating)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/` \u2014 dispatch tool documentation needs new tool added\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- dispatch_wave_start \u2014 exists, no change\\n- dispatch_item_status \u2014 exists, no change\\n- dispatch_wave_status \u2014 exists, no change\\n- dispatch_spawn \u2014 exists, no change\\n- dispatch_create_plan \u2014 MISSING, needs creation\\n- dispatch_read \u2014 exists, reads plans, no change\\n\\n### Tests needed\\n\\n- New test for `dispatch_create_plan` MCP tool\\n- Integration test: groom-milestone Step 9 \u2192 dispatch_create_plan \u2192 dispatch_wave_start flow\\n\\n## Fact Check Summary Re Groomed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims checked: 4\\nVERIFIED: 3 | REFUTED: 1\\n\\n### Claim 1 (original): SKILL.md documents wrong write_dispatch_plan signature verbatim\\nStatus: REFUTED\\nEvidence: SKILL.md Step 9 does not contain `write_dispatch_plan(milestone, conflict_groups, waves, quality_gates)`. It references `dispatch_wave_start` MCP tool for wave registration.\\n\\n### Claim 2 (reframed): No MCP tool exists for dispatch plan creation/writing\\nStatus: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: dispatch-tools-researcher searched all MCP tool definitions in plugins/development-harness/. Four dispatch tools exist (dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn). None creates/writes the dispatch plan itself. The Python function `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path)` in yaml_writer.py has no MCP wrapper.\\n\\n### Claim 3: SKILL.md Step 9 correctly uses dispatch_wave_start\\nStatus: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: skill-step9-reader confirmed Step 9 instructs calling dispatch_wave_start per wave for state registration.\\n\\n### Claim 4: P986 delivered dispatch orchestration MCP tools\\nStatus: VERIFIED\\nEvidence: dispatch-tools-researcher confirmed P986 delivered all 4 planned tools backed by SQLite persistence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dispatch Mcp Tools Research\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Existing Dispatch MCP Tools (All Implemented in P986)\\n\\nFour dispatch-related MCP tools are now available in the backlog server (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`):\\n\\n1. **`dispatch_wave_start`**\\n   - Parameters: `milestone: int`, `wave_num: int`, `items: list[dict[str, object]]` (each item has 'issue' and 'title')\\n   - Returns: dict with `milestone`, `wave_num`, `items_count`, `status`, `messages`, `warnings`, `errors`\\n   - Behavior: Creates a wave entry and initializes all items with `status=pending` in SQLite\\n   - Persistence: Writes to `~/.dh/projects/{project-slug}/dispatch-state.db`\\n\\n2. **`dispatch_item_status`**\\n   - Parameters: `milestone: int`, `issue: int`, `status: str` (must be 'complete', 'failed', or 'skipped'), `result: str = \\\"\\\"`, `error: str = \\\"\\\"`, `cost: float | None = None`\\n   - Returns: dict with `milestone`, `issue`, `wave_num`, `status`, `messages`, `warnings`, `errors` (or `error` key on failure)\\n   - Behavior: Records completion/failure of a single dispatch item by looking up the item across all waves by milestone+issue pair, then calling appropriate state manager method\\n   - Note: This is a WRITE endpoint for spawned sessions to report back, not a query endpoint\\n   - Persistence: Updates SQLite item row with status, result/error, and completion timestamp\\n\\n3. **`dispatch_wave_status`**\\n   - Parameters: `milestone: int`, `wave_num: int`\\n   - Returns: dict with `DispatchWaveSummary` fields: `milestone`, `wave_num`, `status`, `total_items`, `pending`, `in_progress`, `complete`, `failed`, `skipped`, `started_at`, `completed_at`, `elapsed_seconds`, `items` (array), `messages`, `warnings`, `errors`\\n   - Behavior: Queries wave progress, checks for stale PIDs (marks dead processes as failed), returns per-item detail\\n   - No persistence change (read-only query)\\n\\n4. **`dispatch_spawn`** (Background Task)\\n   - Decorator: `@mcp.tool(task=True)` \u2014 runs as a FastMCP background task\\n   - Parameters: `milestone: int`, `wave_num: int` (starting wave), `ctx: Context`, `max_concurrent: int = 3`, `model: str = \\\"sonnet\\\"`, `phase: str = \\\"work\\\"` (either 'groom' or 'work')\\n   - Returns: dict with `DispatchSpawnSummary` fields on completion\\n   - Behavior: Reads dispatch plan YAML, spawns parallel items via `spawn.py` script, monitors PIDs, reads result files, reports progress via `ctx.report_progress()`, detects stale PIDs\\n   - Persistence: Creates wave entries (if not already existing), updates item status and results via state manager\\n\\n### State Persistence Backend\\n\\n- **Database location**: `~/.dh/projects/{project-slug}/dispatch-state.db` (SQLite)\\n- **Schema**: Two tables (`waves` and `items`) with composite primary keys:\\n  - `waves(milestone, wave_num)` \u2192 stores wave-level state\\n  - `items(milestone, wave_num, issue)` \u2192 stores per-item state\\n- **Manager class**: `DispatchStateManager` in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` (NEW FILE)\\n- **Key methods**: `create_wave()`, `set_item_in_progress()`, `set_item_complete()`, `set_item_failed()`, `get_wave()`, `get_all_waves()`, `get_item()`, `check_stale_pids()`\\n- **All methods synchronous**; called from async server code via `asyncio.to_thread()`\\n\\n### What P986 Planned vs What Exists\\n\\n**Planned (all achieved)**:\\n- Four MCP tools: dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_spawn \u2713\\n- SQLite state backend at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/dispatch-state.db` \u2713\\n- DispatchStateManager class with required methods \u2713\\n- FastMCP v3 background task support via `@mcp.tool(task=True)` \u2713\\n- Five Pydantic data models (DispatchItemRecord, DispatchWaveRecord, DispatchSpawnResult, DispatchWaveSummary, DispatchSpawnSummary) \u2713\\n- Unit tests (test_dispatch_state.py: 27 tests) \u2713\\n- Integration tests (test_dispatch_tools.py: 17 tests) \u2713\\n\\n**Status**: All tasks in P986 marked complete (T01, T03, T04, T05, T06)\\n\\n### Gap Analysis: What Orchestrator Needs to Use MCP Tools Directly\\n\\n**What exists**:\\n- All four MCP tools are fully functional and tested\\n- State persistence via SQLite is implemented\\n- Progress reporting via FastMCP context is functional\\n\\n**Gap: No dispatch plan GENERATION tool**:\\n- `dispatch_spawn` reads an existing dispatch plan YAML from disk\\n- No MCP tool exists to CREATE/WRITE a dispatch plan YAML\\n- Orchestrator must either:\\n  1. Call `dispatch_schema.write_dispatch_plan()` Python function directly (not via MCP), or\\n  2. Have a new MCP tool `dispatch_plan_write()` that wraps that function\\n\\n**Related existing tools that complement dispatch**:\\n- `dispatch_read` (existing, reads plan from disk)\\n- `dispatch_validate` (existing, validates plan structure)\\n- `dispatch_stale_check` (existing, detects added/removed issues)\\n- `dispatch_conflicts` (existing, analyzes Impact Radius conflicts)\\n\\n**Missing tool**: A write/create endpoint for dispatch plans. Currently the orchestrator must call Python functions directly or use the SAM CLI (`sam` command). The `/work-milestone` skill orchestrates this via direct Python calls, not MCP tools.\\n\\n### Known Issues (From P986 Context Notes)\\n\\n1. **`_poll_until_done` infinite loop**: No timeout on PID polling loop \u2014 long-running or zombie processes block indefinitely. Needs follow-up backlog item with `max_wait_seconds` parameter.\\n2. **Result truncation violation**: `content[:4096]` at server.py line 2307 truncates result before storing. Violates \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" repository rule. Needs follow-up backlog item.\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nThe dispatch orchestration system is feature-complete for state management and task execution. The four core MCP tools are production-ready and tested. The main gap for full MCP-based orchestration is the lack of a dispatch plan WRITE tool \u2014 dispatch plan generation still requires direct Python function calls.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Skill Md Currently Says Step 9\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Lines 77-78** (Step 9 in the Mermaid flowchart):\\n```\\nWavePlan[\\\"Step 9: Build Dispatch Plan<br>Action: Assign items to waves.<br>Wave 1: all items with no dependencies and no conflict group overlap.<br>Wave 2: items unblocked after Wave 1. Continue until all items assigned.<br>Verify wave ordering and dependency references before writing.<br>Call dispatch_wave_start per wave to register state.<br>Output: plan/milestone-{N}-dispatch.yaml\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n**Line 98** (MCP Tools section):\\n```\\nThe dispatch plan YAML is written by the orchestrator using the schema defined in [./references/dispatch-plan-schema.md](./references/dispatch-plan-schema.md). The conflict analysis and wave assignment logic (Steps 5\u20139) runs in-session \u2014 it does not call external module functions.\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Is Currently Described\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nStep 9 says:\\n1. Assign items to waves following dependency and conflict group rules\\n2. Verify wave ordering and dependency references before writing\\n3. **Call dispatch_wave_start per wave to register state**\\n4. Output: `plan/milestone-{N}-dispatch.yaml`\\n\\nThe schema documentation (dispatch-plan-schema.md) confirms the YAML is written by the orchestrator using the schema, and that `dispatch_wave_start` is called per wave.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Should Be Happening\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe current instructions are CORRECT. Step 9 DOES say to call `dispatch_wave_start` per wave. Line 95 in the MCP Tools section explicitly states:\\n\\n```\\ndispatch_wave_start(milestone, wave_num, items)` \u2014 Step 9: registers each wave in the dispatch state database before writing the plan YAML; use to initialise state alongside the file artifact\\n```\\n\\nThe in-session wave assignment logic and file writing are both properly documented as Step 9 responsibilities.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Disconnect Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe premise in the backlog item description appears incorrect. The SKILL.md already documents that:\\n- Step 9 calls `dispatch_wave_start` per wave \u2713\\n- The dispatch plan YAML is written by the orchestrator \u2713\\n- MCP dispatch tools are explicitly referenced \u2713\\n\\nNo changes are needed to Step 9 instructions. The skill already directs the orchestrator to use MCP dispatch tools as part of Step 9 execution.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius Refuted Bug Claim\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Finding Summary\\n\\n**Status: FALSE ALARM** \u2014 The bug report claims groom-milestone/SKILL.md Step 9 documents the wrong function signature `write_dispatch_plan(milestone, conflict_groups, waves, quality_gates)`. Investigation reveals:\\n\\n1. **SKILL.md does NOT document any `write_dispatch_plan` function signature**\\n2. Step 9 (lines 77-78 in Mermaid) describes workflow operations only\\n3. The only function referenced in Step 9 is `dispatch_wave_start(milestone, wave_num, items)` (correct)\\n4. SKILL.md line 98 states: \\\"The dispatch plan YAML is written by the orchestrator using the schema defined in [./references/dispatch-plan-schema.md]\\\" \u2014 no explicit function call\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (define write_dispatch_plan)\\n\\n**dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py::write_dispatch_plan** (line 63)\\n- Correct signature: `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) -> Path`\\n- Public API exported via dispatch_schema.__init__.py\\n- Serializes DispatchPlan model to YAML with kebab-case keys\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (call write_dispatch_plan)\\n\\n**scripts/gen_milestone_2_dispatch.py** (line 104)\\n- Calls: `write_dispatch_plan(plan, output_path)`\\n- Usage is CORRECT \u2014 passes DispatchPlan object and Path\\n\\n**plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_yaml_writer.py** (16+ test cases)\\n- All calls: `write_dispatch_plan(plan, target)`\\n- All tests use CORRECT signature\\n- Tests verify kebab-case output, atomic rename, symlink rejection, directory creation\\n\\n### Documentation Files Checked\\n\\n| File | Contains wrong signature? | Notes |\\n|------|---------------------------|-------|\\n| groom-milestone/SKILL.md | NO | References dispatch_wave_start; YAML writing described at line 98 without explicit function call |\\n| dispatch-plan-schema.md | NO | Focuses on YAML field schema; does not reference function |\\n| dispatch_schema/__init__.py | NO | Exports function in __all__; no docstring to contain signature |\\n| groom-milestone/references/* | NO | No other references found |\\n\\n### Systems Inventory (all files checked)\\n\\nFiles searched:\\n- dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py \u2014 Producer (correct)\\n- dispatch_schema/__init__.py \u2014 Public API (correct)\\n- dispatch_schema/readers/yaml_reader.py \u2014 Reader (not producer)\\n- dispatch_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Model definitions\\n- scripts/gen_milestone_2_dispatch.py \u2014 Consumer (correct)\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_yaml_writer.py \u2014 16+ test cases (all correct)\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py \u2014 Dispatch tooling tests\\n- groom-milestone/SKILL.md \u2014 Skill documentation (no wrong signature found)\\n- dispatch-plan-schema.md \u2014 Schema reference (correct)\\n\\n### Recommendation\\n\\n**This bug report should be closed as INVALID.** The claimed wrong signature does not exist in the codebase. Possible causes:\\n- Confusion with `dispatch_wave_start(milestone, wave_num, items)` documented in Step 9\\n- Reference to historical code no longer in the repository\\n- Misunderstanding of the SKILL.md workflow description as containing a Python function signature\\n\\nAll actual code that calls `write_dispatch_plan` uses the correct signature. No fixes are required.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (define write_dispatch_plan)\\n\\n**dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py::write_dispatch_plan** (line 63)\\n- Current signature: `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) -> Path`\\n- Serializes DispatchPlan model to YAML with kebab-case keys and atomic rename\\n- Public API exported via dispatch_schema.__init__.py (line 29)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (call write_dispatch_plan)\\n\\n**scripts/gen_milestone_2_dispatch.py::main** (line 104)\\n- Calls `write_dispatch_plan(plan, output_path)` with correct (actual) signature\\n- Already using correct interface: passes DispatchPlan object + Path\\n\\n**plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_yaml_writer.py** (multiple test cases)\\n- All 16+ test cases call `write_dispatch_plan(plan, target)` with correct signature\\n- Tests verify kebab-case output, atomic rename, symlink rejection, directory creation\\n- All tests already using correct interface\\n\\n### Documentation \u2014 Wrong Signature (MAIN ISSUE)\\n\\n**plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md** (Step 9, line 77)\\n- Wrong signature documented: `write_dispatch_plan(milestone, conflict_groups, waves, quality_gates)`\\n- Actually described in lines 77-78: \\\"Call dispatch_wave_start per wave to register state. Output: plan/milestone-{N}-dispatch.yaml\\\"\\n- The description does NOT actually include a function signature statement \u2014 this is a workflow description of Step 9\\n- Reference: The SKILL.md does NOT document Python function signatures; it describes workflow operations\\n- **Clarification**: No explicit wrong signature found in SKILL.md Step 9. The step describes workflow operations (calling dispatch_wave_start, writing YAML). No Python call syntax documented.\\n\\n### Documentation \u2014 Related (may reference the function)\\n\\n**plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md** (line 1-155)\\n- Documents the schema structure and field definitions\\n- Does NOT reference or document the write_dispatch_plan function\\n- Focused on the YAML format, not the API\\n\\n### Public API Exports (no breaking changes needed here)\\n\\n**dispatch_schema/__init__.py** (lines 29, 54)\\n- Exports `write_dispatch_plan` in __all__\\n- Does NOT document the signature (good practice \u2014 users import and call)\\n- No docstring changes needed in __init__.py\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| File | Role | Uses Function | Status | Action |\\n|------|------|--|--------|--------|\\n| dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py | Producer \u2014 defines function | Defines | Correct (plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path) | None |\\n| dispatch_schema/__init__.py | Public API \u2014 re-exports | Exports in __all__ | Correct | None |\\n| scripts/gen_milestone_2_dispatch.py | Consumer \u2014 calls function | Calls write_dispatch_plan(plan, output_path) | Correct usage | None |\\n| test_yaml_writer.py | Test consumer \u2014 calls function | Calls write_dispatch_plan(plan, target) | Correct usage \u2014 16+ tests passing | None |\\n| groom-milestone/SKILL.md | Workflow doc \u2014 describes Step 9 | Does NOT document signature | No signature documented in Step 9 | Verify backlog item description |\\n| dispatch-plan-schema.md | Schema reference | Does NOT reference function | Correct \u2014 focuses on YAML structure | None |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n**Finding**: The bug report claims groom-milestone/SKILL.md Step 9 documents a wrong signature, but inspection shows:\\n1. Step 9 (lines 77-78) describes workflow operations, not Python signatures\\n2. No explicit function signature documented in SKILL.md\\n3. All actual code consumers (scripts/gen_milestone_2_dispatch.py and all tests) use the correct signature\\n4. The wrong signature documented does NOT appear in the repository\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: The bug report may reference an older version of SKILL.md or a different location. Recommend: verify backlog item #1013 description for clarification on where the wrong signature appears.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P1013-hook-validation-test.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:35:21Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"83d353dbd582c577a5ae4b4480916d60dfe7aa3ee22c3de6b527429b6fb3f8d8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWWKSg\"}"}